extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 51-53 (cache p052-p054, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the cache and checked against renders of printed 52 and 53, where the powers, skill list and equipment sit. The entry starts at The Earth Child R.C.C. heading on printed 51 (after the shared Children of the Earth & Stars introduction) and ends at Cybernetics & Bionics on printed 53, above The Star Child heading. || CATEGORY: headed R.C.C. twice; printed 51 says the transformation makes the character a creature of magic. A race, so no occ_group and men_of_arms false; it prints its own related and secondary skills, stored as printed. || XP: the column headed Dubugghs, Earth & Star Child (so spelled) on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render. Every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: human-form hit points not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s other classes. P.P.E. is P.E. x2 with no gain by level (power 10, which says star child on this page, a misprint). I.S.P. is M.E. + 4D6, +1D6+1 per level. || STONE FORM: the 40 M.D.C. per level belongs to the stone form only, so it is not mdc_base, which would make the human form a mega-damage being too; second_form carries S.D.C. and hit points only. The form and its powers are special abilities in prose. || BONUSES: printed 52 heads the numbered powers with only applicable when transformed, but the list includes P.P.E. and life span, so power 11''s bonuses are read as the character''s and stored: +1 initiative, +3 roll with impact, +2 vs horror factor, +2 vs magic on spell_magic and ritual_magic. || PSIONICS: major; eight powers from the Physical category, usable in either form. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Track Animals is the catalog Track & Trap Animals; Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic. English has no language row and rides Language: Other at the printed 65% (row ruling, 2026-11-12: no language skill rows); two languages of choice at +15% are a two-pick Language: Other group. Science is two entries, Botany at +10% and the rest at +5%; Pilot any is read to include the Horsemanship category at +5%. Hand to Hand: Expert is granted; Assassin if evil, no price printed: costs { assassin: 0 }. || EQUIPMENT: rope and/or nylon cord stored as nylon cord, spikes as iron spikes, pouches or sacks as one pouch, wooden staff or walking stick as a walking stick. Not stored: weapons of choice (none named), heavy body armor and a pet (traditional, not issued)."
