# Earth Child

## Lore

The earth child draws on the mystic energy that flows through the planet along ley lines and through every living thing, and believes that power comes from the living spirit of the Earth. With a thought he becomes a twelve-foot giant of stone. Like the druids he holds life, nature and freedom in high regard, but he is no teacher or priest: earth children are nomads and adventurers who take action against injustice to life or land. They are usually excellent wilderness scouts and huntsmen who never kill for pleasure or hunt more than is needed.

## GM Notes

Children of the earth come from one human clan, the Tarramar of the Island of Mann, about 2000 strong. Raised from infancy in the clan''s teachings, most master the transformation by age six; a child of one ordinary parent may inherit it only with major psionic powers and the clan''s teaching, and blooms late. Beings without honor (destroyers of the land and enslavers of life) may, to an earth child, be treated without mercy. Most are drawn to heavy weapons and wear heavy brown, tan or camouflage armor, and many keep a dog, fox, wolf, bear, wild cat, falcon or eagle.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'earth-child');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'earth-child';

